{"id":"40c179ab-272d-4322-bcc5-7df3740c579f","object":"chat.completion","created":1785028507,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    segments = case['segments']\\n    budget = case['budget']\\n    n = len(segments)\\n    names = [s['name'] for s in segments]\\n    mins = [s['minimum'] for s in segments]\\n    caps = [s['capacity'] for s in segments]\\n    imp = [s['importance'] for s in segments]\\n    alloc = mins[:]\\n    remaining = budget - sum(alloc)\\n    # assume budget is valid (>= sum(mins) and <= sum(caps))\\n    while remaining > 0:\\n        best = -1\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            if alloc[i] < caps[i]:\\n                if best == -1:\\n                    best = i\\n                else:\\n                    # compare importance/(alloc+1) using cross multiplication\\n                    left = imp[i] * (alloc[best] + 1)\\n                    right = imp[best] * (alloc[i] + 1)\\n                    if left > right or (left == right and i < best):\\n                        best = i\\n        alloc[best] += 1\\n        remaining -= 1\\n    by_name = dict(zip(names, alloc))\\n    return {\\n        'allocations': alloc,\\n        'by_name': by_name,\\n        'total': budget\\n    }\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that returns an object with allocations, by_name, total according to the schema. The case is a payload with segments list (each with name, importance, minimum, capacity) and budget. The algorithm: start each segment at its minimum. Then allocate remaining budget one token at a time to segment with max importance/(current allocated+1) (since next position is current+1). Tie break by original segment order (index). Continue until budget exhausted. Return allocations list (list of ints in same order as segments), by_name dict mapping segment names to allocations, total (must equal budget). Also ensure total budget >