andle? while remaining > 0: best_idx = -1; best_val = None; for i in range(n): if alloc[i] < cap[i]: next_pos = alloc[i] + 1; val = (imp[i], -next_pos, i) # minimizing? Actually we want max importance/next_pos. So use negative. Or use tuple: (-imp[i], next_pos, i) for min? Simpler: compute fraction using cross multiplication. For each i, compute candidate = (imp[i], next_pos, i). Use comparison function: a > b if a[0]*b[1] > b[0]*a[1]. Or use fractions.Fraction to avoid errors. Write helper: def better(i, j): return imp[i] * (alloc[j]+1) > imp[j] * (alloc[i]+1). Then select best. Tie break by original index (i). For equal ratio, lower index wins. So if better(i, best_idx) or (equal and i < best_idx) then update. But careful with best_idx initial. We'll loop to find max. For each i where alloc[i] < cap[i], compute if best_idx==-1 or better(i, best_idx) or (imp[i]*(alloc[best_idx]+1) == imp[best_idx]*(alloc[i]+1) and i < best_idx): best_idx = i. Then alloc[best_idx]+=1; remaining-=1. After loop, allocations = alloc; by_name = dict(zip(names, alloc)); total = budget. Return dict.\n\nBut we must ensure that by_name keys exactly match segment names as strings. Use dict.\n\nEdge: if budget exactly sum(minimum) then no loop, allocations = min.\n\nAlso need to import nothing? Use standard library.\n\nWrite source code as string.\n\nNow produce JSON output with key \"implementation\". Ensure proper escaping.\n\nMake sure not to include any extra text."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1384,"completion_tokens":1332,"total_tokens":2716,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1280},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1023},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1280,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":104},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}